      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T14:52:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, the motivation behind this patch is to enable us to build Arm64 assembly files when building for a host x86_64. The relevant patch is https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680026/12 while the discussion [here](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680026/comment/853357e8_6c48f2ca/) should give some more detail as to why we need to do this.\n\nTo echo Ulya, this feature (the ART simulator) is only used in development and is a special mode that needs to be explicitly enabled by the ART developer. If a compiler update causes a regression, this will only break the simulator and not regular (debug or production) builds of ART.",
      "parentUuid": "2c2ebb93_43375370",
      "revId": "99fd863014bffe145d795858c4a5c01a5d44e47c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
